# Taiga-First Development (33pol)

**All ideation, planning, development, and implementation for this project go through Taiga.** Use the **user-taiga** MCP server only — not internal todo lists, not ad-hoc markdown backlogs.

Read tool schemas under `mcps/user-taiga/tools/` before each `CallMcpTool`. Prefer `projectSlug` + refs (`taskRef`, `issueRef`, `storyRef`) over internal IDs.

## Resolve project (every session)

1. Project name = workspace folder basename (`33pol`) or root `package.json` / `*.csproj` name.
2. `taiga_list_projects` → match slug/name (case-insensitive) → store `projectSlug`.
3. No match → ask user to create a Taiga project; do not pick another project.

## Core MCP tools (use these)

### Sprints (= milestones in Taiga API)

| Action | Tool |
|--------|------|
| List | `taiga_list_milestones` |
| Read | `taiga_get_milestone` |
| Create | `taiga_create_milestone` (`name`, `slug`, `estimatedStart`, `estimatedFinish`) |
| Update | `taiga_update_milestone` |

Assign work to a sprint via `milestoneSlug` or `milestoneId` on stories/tasks/issues. Reorder backlog: `taiga_update_story_sprint_order`.

### Tasks

| Action | Tool |
|--------|------|
| List | `taiga_list_tasks` |
| Read | `taiga_get_task`, `taiga_get_task_history` |
| Create | `taiga_create_task` (link with `userStoryId`) |
| Update | `taiga_update_task` (`statusName`, assignee, milestone, etc.) |
| Comment | `taiga_comment_on_task` |
| Close/remove | `taiga_archive_task`, `taiga_delete_task` |

### Issues (bugs, defects, questions)

| Action | Tool |
|--------|------|
| List | `taiga_list_issues` |
| Read | `taiga_get_issue`, `taiga_get_issue_history` |
| Create | `taiga_create_issue` (`typeName: Bug` when applicable) |
| Update | `taiga_update_issue` |
| Comment | `taiga_comment_on_issue` |
| Close/remove | `taiga_archive_issue`, `taiga_delete_issue` |

Helpers: `taiga_list_statuses`, `taiga_list_issue_types`, `taiga_search` (dedupe before create).

### Stories & epics (feature planning)

| Entity | Create | Update | Comment |
|--------|--------|--------|---------|
| User story | `taiga_create_story` | `taiga_update_story` | `taiga_comment_on_story` |
| Epic | `taiga_create_epic` | `taiga_update_epic` | `taiga_comment_on_epic` |

List: `taiga_list_user_stories`, `taiga_list_epics`.

## When to use Taiga

| Phase | Taiga action |
|-------|----------------|
| **Ideation** | Search existing items; capture ideas as story/epic + comments; create milestone if new sprint |
| **Planning** | Decompose story → tasks; set sprint, status, acceptance criteria in descriptions |
| **Implementation** | One task/issue in progress; comment progress; close when verified |
| **Bugs** | `taiga_create_issue` first → fix → comment root cause → close issue |

Skip Taiga only if the user explicitly says so, or pure Q&A with no project work.

## Mandatory workflows

### New feature

1. `taiga_search` → avoid duplicates.
2. Epic (if multi-sprint) → story → tasks (`userStoryId`).
3. Brief user: project slug, story/task refs, order.
4. Per task: `taiga_update_task` in-progress → code → test → `taiga_comment_on_task` → done.
5. Close story when all tasks done.

### Bug fix

1. `taiga_create_issue` (repro, expected vs actual, env, file paths).
2. `taiga_update_issue` in-progress → fix → `taiga_comment_on_issue` → closed.

### Sprint work

1. `taiga_list_milestones` — pick or `taiga_create_milestone` for new sprint.
2. Assign stories/tasks with `milestoneSlug` on create/update.
3. Track sprint progress via task/issue status updates, not side channels.

## Task quality

- One concern per task; testable done criteria in description.
- ≤ ~half day each; split if larger.
- Order: models → API → UI.

## Status discipline

- In-progress in Taiga **before** editing code.
- Park or close when switching items; never leave stale in-progress.
- Close only after build/tests pass when applicable.

## User communication

Start: **Taiga project**, **refs**, **current task/issue/sprint**.  
Finish: what was closed in Taiga and what remains.
